{"title":"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Similar_to_Solution_3)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Similar to Solution 3)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(easy_to_understand)_by_Power_Solve\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (easy to understand) by Power Solve</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2_(🚀_Under_3_min_🚀)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2 (🚀 Under 3 min 🚀)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> lie on the graph of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/2/da24aea6721e5aed46a0745d6469dd8edf0c1ba5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\log_{2}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"80\" height=\"19\" />. The midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/7/c17384a6c2a4aee0ea47051a974ad1cb5967d47f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />. What is the positive difference between the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-coordinates of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/a/23a88f20fb1c0d35e2d15f336b11e2724fbb8713.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}~2\\sqrt{11}\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}~4\\sqrt{3}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}~8\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}~4\\sqrt{5}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}~9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"433\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/3/cc324292edd5c9f3a003697229b17e13186b6bba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A(6+m,2+n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"127\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/1/d0176eced92625ec6706036a00c3e910a7cedbc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B(6-m,2-n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"128\" height=\"20\" />, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/8/49872c1a93c707dd850a4c311b1e6eadacc58500.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> is their midpoint. Thus, we must find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/3/c93d829d38f1f73cd97c8fd926e636e968d0c158.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2m$\" width=\"24\" height=\"12\" />. We find two equations due to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/6/5f642cbbd390b4882363ab6b5c2906dbf6be6cc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> both lying on the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/2/da24aea6721e5aed46a0745d6469dd8edf0c1ba5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\log_{2}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"80\" height=\"19\" />. The two equations are then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/2/012bebfe9c324b4aefcd9714164c9d4f07e8bfc4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{2}(6+m)=2+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"161\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/9/239d612530845d066df95dc524687d4d3e63c2f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{2}(6-m)=2-n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"161\" height=\"20\" />. Now add these two equations to obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d170963d18ce6290516f7976bd81f52a0e7ef06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{2}(6+m)+\\log_{2}(6-m)=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"242\" height=\"20\" />. By logarithm rules, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/f/e6f4ac40e3395879d51873e7595f6243f2c44472.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{2}((6+m)(6-m))=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"203\" height=\"20\" />. By raising 2 to the power of  both sides, we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/4/65404e0273c349738ba54189e9f33350f04b18bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6+m)(6-m)=16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"167\" height=\"20\" />. We then get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/9/4e9b98ecdc02981e01731997578bf2da00d867bf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[36-m^2=16 \\rightarrow m^2=20 \\rightarrow m=2\\sqrt{5}\\]\" width=\"302\" height=\"18\" />. Since we're looking for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/3/c93d829d38f1f73cd97c8fd926e636e968d0c158.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2m$\" width=\"24\" height=\"12\" />, we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/9/02925a69df12d9d1b700c5d0c29b45b9b36993fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2)(2\\sqrt{5})=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }4\\sqrt{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"177\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p>~amcrunner (yay, my first AMC solution)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/c/85c9fbd681fe4e2a45dadb189e6c22d262003a8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x_A + x_B}{2} = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"104\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/4/5d4f20fc41c8ada1a589ecdb8870c4a7f6040a34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\log_2 x_A + \\log_2 x_B}{2} = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"172\" height=\"39\" />. The first equation becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a4e5a8bed542a191eb1597ffbd4f9daa3801414.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_A + x_B = 12,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"17\" /> and the second becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/5/8952ba57a0fe4396fe51f0b280d70add3ad1021d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_2(x_A x_B) = 4,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"128\" height=\"20\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/b/dab788c410ab1fd7a494381269efe71d3bbaa4a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_A x_B = 16.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"92\" height=\"17\" />\nThen\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/9/aa977f6a53b91449822e1f1631167118fdd169df.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\left| x_A - x_B \\right| &amp; = \\sqrt{\\left( x_A + x_B \\right)^2 - 4 x_A x_B} \\\\ &amp; = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 4 \\sqrt{5}}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"277\" height=\"71\" />\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (Professor Chen Education Palace, www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Basically, we can use the midpoint formula \n</p><p>assume that the points are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/5/b354638f824de285dce6d6d3f72163cb287aeff7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_1,y_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/1/871e8d2e83189f86381352faa5c18c2d0cf3f3b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_2,y_2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>assume that the points are (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/ccada11db7b2b90693e2fac4f887a57fce6f96bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb85647ef6cf67dbb541df97e1282abea26c1dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{2}(x_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"65\" height=\"20\" />) and (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7d010bbff66a0c41e43310a51efbaa6bf63396.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/a/4dac1107d2c3cf53d865cfc5e3397ce6957e25e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{2}(x_2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"65\" height=\"20\" />)\n</p><p><br />\nmidpoint formula is (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/0/070f50e0de9808873273b45dd525f0ffec202844.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x_1+x_2}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"64\" height=\"37\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/4/43461970754ace307b3bd2d05620f62341b3b17b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\log_{2}(x_1)+\\log_{2}(x_2)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"154\" height=\"40\" />)\n</p><p><br />\nthus\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/8/6b8c66e39d23d1aa281760c63f8e3b4ff768aff7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1+x_2=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/c/f3c8a7cc3d8d07ba6a7161085dbb6ba52d4698c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_2=12-x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"17\" />\nand \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/d/36da2f262e3c063e25fbc44cadb6c78a4222a01d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{2}(x_1)+\\log_{2}(x_2)=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"183\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/a/a6a4097ef0a0d51ad3aa7502f3353e02e8866c20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{2}(x_1)+\\log_{2}(12-x_1)=\\log_{2}(16)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"278\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/4/d3417f7c7829cd7c00447a117800dc020b691d3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{2}((12x_1-x_1^2)/16)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"198\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>since\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/8/3688876ff545b6900b80c429336386b50e4a4326.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^0=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" />\nso,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/f/b5f3f1b26db1bfb9b8ec99f13f1248bbef34422d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12x_1-x_1^2=16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"120\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/2/192d256f3c286d5bc180abae66210f8a8f2093ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12x_1-x_1^2-16=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"152\" height=\"21\" />\nfor simplicity lets say <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/e/0fee9bdd7fad2356bbee739f26edb3fada8470a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"10\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/6/a2669e64d1763b56e2471708310709c1ceb7fa90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12x-x^2=16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"113\" height=\"18\" />. We rearrange to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/3/223cf8b4b3b25b91de76f0719ce94145222094ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2-12x+16=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>put this into quadratic formula and you should get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/f/7cfcaa2900900be74bc71bb8a04dcf9f6eee0a6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1=6+2\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"22\" />\nTherefore,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/8/e28e851481e5d12ecd055bea62bb04db51bd0453.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1=6+2\\sqrt{5}-(6-2\\sqrt{5})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"210\" height=\"24\" />\n</p><p>which equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/b/a8bde8452df3c50d98541731e05063db39d32ea5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6-6+4\\sqrt{5}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }4\\sqrt{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"203\" height=\"35\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Similar to above, but solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/2/f520f9ab3076c2c8e33c2c226b87a515126a2a9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 2^y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"14\" /> in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/9/7e9691d7ddf36a0a980075ffce939a36b28e5e55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2^{y}+2^{2+(2-y)})/2= 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"168\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/1/79166d1aa198dd12472892f2f2fe24219919a03e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^y + 2^{4-y} = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"118\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/2/5925c408cfb4cba8fe93fae44963ec90fc7a058c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2^y)^2 + 2^4 = 12(2^y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"153\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/c/becc2a2135d2bddae126160efb39c70d02240f87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 -12x + 16 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Distance between roots of the quadratic is the discriminant: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b00920bd09198ae6993d60dc8d8a16f6e765023.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{{12}^2 - 4(1)(16)} = \\sqrt{80} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }4\\sqrt{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"294\" height=\"36\" />\n</p><p>~oinava\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Similar_to_Solution_3.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Similar_to_Solution_3)\">Solution 5 (Similar to Solution 3)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Similar to Solution 3)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the two points on the curve <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/2/88285d094fda7a7e73155f4a39361071788cd0af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\log_2 x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"80\" height=\"19\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26e728c9c9da0017da9db7920514df01b783c3ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A(x_1, \\log_2 x_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"107\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d7aec69a24a5183fd587043d3f4c7db1b759c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B(x_2, \\log_2 x_2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"108\" height=\"20\" />. By the midpoint formula, the coordinates of the midpoint are given by:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/0/1e0a9ac272a4900f84ba6dfc461f1645792f0488.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left( \\frac{x_1 + x_2}{2}, \\frac{\\log_2 x_1 + \\log_2 x_2}{2} \\right)\\]\" width=\"219\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Given that the midpoint is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/7/c17384a6c2a4aee0ea47051a974ad1cb5967d47f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, we obtain the following system of equations:\n\\begin{align}\nx_1 + x_2 &amp;= 12 \\\\\n\\log_2(x_1 x_2) &amp;= 4 \\implies x_1 x_2 = 16\n\\end{align}\n</p><p>By Vieta's formulas, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/ccada11db7b2b90693e2fac4f887a57fce6f96bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7d010bbff66a0c41e43310a51efbaa6bf63396.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> are the roots of the quadratic equation:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/6/e663bcb46fff9b1c553d3b29b64eb441d62e8b8e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2 - 12x + 16 = 0\\]\" width=\"141\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>Solving via the quadratic formula yields the roots:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/f/9bf05fdaad628fe2e465e991604bd68b96fa2e09.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = \\frac{12 \\pm \\sqrt{144 - 64}}{2} = 6 \\pm 2\\sqrt{5}\\]\" width=\"250\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>Without loss of generality, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/7/e376f3cab4f89321ad59e161860383c1ea4d0229.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 = 6 + 2\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"22\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/a/3aac562370615826d18b9ea2e03f1e9a5389d329.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_2 = 6 - 2\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"22\" />. The horizontal distance between the two points is:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/3/3136269b9b27d9c5b40cf77a8e84df896f9c367f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|x_1 - x_2| = (6 + 2\\sqrt{5}) - (6 - 2\\sqrt{5}) = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 4\\sqrt{5}} \\quad \\blacksquare\\]\" width=\"404\" height=\"33\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28easy_to_understand.29_by_Power_Solve\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(easy_to_understand)_by_Power_Solve\">Video Solution (easy to understand) by Power Solve</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (easy to understand) by Power Solve\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/YXIH3UbLqK8?si=HZSSwpFx7AisyTVm&amp;t=434\">https://youtu.be/YXIH3UbLqK8?si=HZSSwpFx7AisyTVm&amp;t=434</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1\">Video Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/R_OdhW85yUc\">https://youtu.be/R_OdhW85yUc</a>\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (Professor Chen Education Palace, www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_2_.28.F0.9F.9A.80_Under_3_min_.F0.9F.9A.80.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2_(🚀_Under_3_min_🚀)\">Video Solution 2 (🚀 Under 3 min 🚀)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2 (🚀 Under 3 min 🚀)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/DOXmoQlMS7Y\">https://youtu.be/DOXmoQlMS7Y</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A\">2023 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php